  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its detailed design, loss of historic fabric and refuse storage would result in 'less than substantial ' harm to the special architectural and historic interest of the listed building as a designated heritage asset and a part of the Enfield Town Conservation Area. The harm is not outweighed by any sufficient benefits, contrary to Sections 16(2) and 66(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990,  Sections 12 and 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies HC1 of the London Plan (2021); CP30 and CP31 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD37 and DMD44 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), the Enfield Town Conservation Area Management proposals (2015) and Enfield Heritage Strategy 2019 - 2024 (2019)."
